QLite. That is the 2026-11-08 environment-only failure this guard's docstring was written against, now on the pool, where agents are told to run tests (core learning 'When code is added, moved or retired, ask which guards were scoped to the old shape'). Fix: build the guard from every tracked Dockerfile (`git ls-files '*Dockerfile'`) instead of from one path. Its from-the-pin check also has to accept the test image's `uv python install \"$(cat /opt/python-version)\"` form, or be split per image.", "files": [".devcontainer/Dockerfile", "tests/test_one_python.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "The pool's curation selection is a hand-made directory list, unlike CI's, which is derived and guarded", "recommendation": "Scope: class. The list was written out by hand when CI already derives its selection. `.testament.toml` [suites.curation] default_selection names arrt/tests/{unit,integration,contract,eval} and test_scaffold.py. CI runs `pytest tests --ignore=tests/browser`, and tests/test_default_suite_ci_scope.py exists because hand-kept selection lists 'go stale silently in both directions'. If someone adds a test directory or module under arrt/tests (for example arrt/tests/property), a bare `testament run` will not run it and still reports green. AGENTS.md tells agents to trust that report. Routing a path into the new directory is refused, but only when someone names the path. Core learning: 'When building an inventory of routes, operations or requirements, derive it from the thing itself'. Fix one of two ways. Select `arrt/tests` and let addopts and an `--ignore=arrt/tests/browser` do the excluding, checking first that browser-path routing still goes to the browser suite. Or extend the CI-scope guard to read .testament.toml, so every top-level test directory under arrt/tests belongs to exactly one suite or is deliberately excluded (live).", "files": [".testament.toml"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "record-lint: three suite-total test claims in the change record", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Lines 20-22 of .prawduct/changes/testament-onboarding.md copy suite totals (governance 475, contract 223, curation 5,452, browser 1,451). The evidence store already records pass/fail per tree, and nothing reads these figures. The run's other details (the 95 Node-only checks moving from skipped to passed, the roughly 4-minute browser run) are worth keeping. The totals can go.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/testament-onboarding.md"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "CLAUDE.md says testament falls back to the table's commands, but the fallback runs the manifest's", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. CLAUDE.md's new paragraph says the table commands are 'what CI runs and what testament falls back to here'. AGENTS.md says the fallback 'runs the same tests here'. Those are .testament.toml's suite commands (`-c arrt/pyproject.toml --rootdir=. -n 0`, run from the root), not `cd arrt && uv run pytest`. CI's curation leg is also its own invocation (`--ignore=tests/browser`). The cost of being wrong is small, but it would mislead someone comparing a fallback run with a table run. Fix: drop the 'falls back to' clause, or say the fallback runs .testament.toml's commands.", "files": ["CLAUDE.md"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "The pool, its test image and its `-n 0` are not in project-preferences' testing rows", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. project-preferences.md \u00a7 Parallelization still reads '-n auto for the curation suite, in its addopts' as the whole story. The decisions to run all four suites on testament with `-n 0` (testament batches are the parallelism), to use a test image separate from the deploy image, and to keep live markers off the pool have their reasons only in comments in .testament.toml and .devcontainer/Dockerfile and in the change record. The reasons are sound and recorded. They are just not in the artifact that owns testing choices. Fix: add a pointer from that row to .testament.toml, not a copy of the reasons.", "files": [".testament.toml", ".devcontainer/Dockerfile"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog reconciliation: no open item resolved or affected", "recommendation": "Scope: none (mandatory cross-check, no defect). Checked 18 open items. `affecting` returns none for the six changed paths, and none mentions testament, the devcontainer, the pool or Playwright. Priors: the CLAUDE.md length overrun has been accepted repeatedly (R-4 in rev-20261009T012018Z and earlier). This branch takes it from 128 to 137 lines with one paragraph and one clause. That is no material change, so it is not raised again. Records Pass covered .prawduct/changes/testament-onboarding.md (the only oracle file). Apart from the lint NOTE above, its claims hold: the Playwright pin is held by tests/preferences/test_test_image.py, and the deploy image's root test stage is described accurately.", "fid": "R-6"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 2, "note": 4}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 600, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `chore/testament-onboarding`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "ee54a2a2853fa6d28636c8225f583e5f00e3f492", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/changes/testament-onboarding.md", "AGENTS.md", "CLAUDE.md", "docs/testing.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [{"check": "suite-total-claim", "path": ".prawduct/changes/testament-onboarding.md", "line": 20, "detail": "suite-total test claim '475 passed' \u2014 the evidence store records pass/fail per tree; a prose copy drifts and nothing reads it"}, {"check": "suite-total-claim", "path": ".prawduct